  "texts": {
    "preamble": "For The vs State on 17 February, 2025 Author: Suvra Ghosh Bench: Suvra Ghosh 17.02.2025 jb. jdt. C.R.R. 485 of 2025 Re: Suresh Agarwal @ Suresh Kumar Agarwal Mr. Sekhar Kr. Basu Mr. Shiladitya Banerjee Mr. Arnab Chatterjee ...",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that charge- sheet has been submitted against the petitioner under Section 120B/269/273 of the Indian Penal Code. Placing reliance on the authority in Ram Nath vs. State of Uttar Pradesh reported in AIR 2024 Supreme Court 1652, learned counsel submits that in view of the overriding effect of the Food Safety and Standards Act over anything inconsistent therewith contained in any other law for the time being in force, charge-sheet submitted under the provisions of Indian Penal Code is bad in law. The petitioner appears to have made out an arguable case.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that charge- sheet has been submitted against the petitioner under Section 120B/269/273 of the Indian Penal Code. Placing reliance on the authority in Ram Nath vs. State of Uttar Pradesh reported in AIR 2024 Supreme Court 1652, learned counsel submits that in view of the overriding effect of the Food Safety and Standards Act over anything inconsistent therewith contained in any other law for the time being in force, charge-sheet submitted under the provisions of Indian Penal Code is bad in law.",
    "respondent_arguments": "The petitioner appears to have made out an arguable case.",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
